In a previous article, richard@iesd.auc.dk (Richard Flamsholt S0rensen) says:

>
>  Now is really the time to ask: what *is* the dreaded Time-outs for
>Praying?

	A while ago, some source-code-delver looked this up and
posted the answer. I believe he said the timeout was a random
number between a few hundred and a few thousand. (Gee, its a good
thing my memory is so specific, huh? :)
	In practice, I have never had a problem using this technique:
I always wait at least as long as it takes to digest a food ration
between prayers. That is, I pray, wait until I'm hungry, eat a
food ration, (and maybe a corpse or two for good measure), wait
until I'm hungry again, then pray again.
	It would be nice if, in some future version, Priests (maybe
just high-level Priests) got to see their prayer timeouts. Or maybe
some new item could allow any character to see their timeout; 
a Ring of Devotion, say, which could change colors (a la rings of 
warning) to indicate just how happy your deity is with you.
